# Brain Runtime â€” Canonical Architecture

## Core Principle

```yaml
brain_is: "Zeus â€” stateless compute fabric"
brain_is_not: "model storage, tokenizer, session memory, governance"

ownership:
  brain/master: "orchestration layer â€” dispatch, session, outcome"
  fem/hacedle:  "CE execution â€” GGUF I/O, tensor ops, candle inference"
  brain/base:   "ABI â€” BrainKernel + BrainRuntime traits (stable, do not modify)"
  brain/hooks:  "hook registry â€” E4 pass-through, E5 governance"

stateless_guarantee: |
  Brain receives ReasonCtx, returns ReasonResult.
  No internal mutable state between calls.
  Memory (KV cache) is owned by session layer, injected per call.
```

---

## Layer Map

```yaml
layers:
  L0_abi:
    path: brain/base/src/lib.rs
    exports: [BrainKernel, BrainRuntime, ReasonCtx, ReasonResult, AlgoParticle]
    stability: FROZEN â€” no change without CSA+CRD sign-off

  L1_runtime:
    path: brain/runtime/src/lib.rs
    exports: [ZeusRuntime, ZeusRouter, ZeusConfig, CeId]
    ce_dispatch: "classify_complexity() -> CeId::{Algo, Local, Remote}"
    stability: STABLE

  L2_master:
    path: brain/master/src/
    role: "SIO-level orchestration: sio -> InferRequest -> execute -> SioOutcome"
    key_files:
      lib.rs:              "BrainMasterRuntime::execute()"
      inference/engine.rs: "InferenceEngine::infer() â€” THE missing link"
      kernel/hacedle.rs:   "HacedleKernel bridge to fem/hacedle candle chain"
      tokenizer/mod.rs:    "BrainTokenizer â€” MUST use tokenizers crate"
      runtime/kv_cache.rs: "KvCache struct + prefill()"
      runtime/logits.rs:   "TopK sampler"
      provider/gguf/:      "GgufLoader â€” MUST delegate to hacedle::loader_std"

  L3_ce:
    path: fem/hacedle/src/x/
    role: "CE.Hacedle â€” inference ops, OWNED BY hacedle team"
    do_not_duplicate:
      - "loader/gguf/* â€” GGUF parsing"
      - "loader/dequant/* â€” quantization"
      - "provider/candle/* â€” transformer layers, lmhead"
      - "ops/* â€” rmsnorm, rope, silu, attention"
```

---

## Inference Chain (target state)

```text
hace brain prompt "hello" --model qwen.gguf

CLI (brain/cli/src/prompt.rs)
  |  PromptArgs { text, model_path, max_tokens }
  v
BrainMasterRuntime::execute(sio)          [brain/master/src/lib.rs]
  |  extract InferRequest from SIO
  v
InferenceEngine::infer(req)               [brain/master/src/inference/engine.rs]
  |
  +-> GgufLoader::load(model_path)        [brain/master/src/provider/gguf/loader.rs]
  |     DELEGATES TO: hacedle::GgufLoaderStd::load()
  |     OUTPUT: LoadedModel { tensor_index, model_spec, mmap_handle }
  |
  +-> BrainTokenizer::encode(text)        [brain/master/src/tokenizer/mod.rs]
  |     SOURCE: tokenizers crate + GGUF metadata tokens/merges
  |     OUTPUT: Vec<u32>  e.g. "hello" -> [9707]
  |
  +-> KvCache::prefill(token_ids, model)  [brain/master/src/runtime/kv_cache.rs]
  |     ALLOCATES: [n_layers][seq_len][n_kv_heads][head_dim] f32
  |
  +-> HacedleKernel::forward(ctx, kv)    [brain/master/src/kernel/hacedle.rs]
  |     DELEGATES TO: hacedle::candle::{embed, layer[0..n], lmhead}
  |     OUTPUT: logits Vec<f32>[vocab_size]
  |
  +-> Logits::top_k(logits, k=5)         [brain/master/src/runtime/logits.rs]
  |     OUTPUT: Vec<(token_id, score)>
  |
  +-> BrainTokenizer::decode([next_id])
        OUTPUT: " world"

SioOutcome { tokens: [9707, 1917], text: "hello world", latency_ms: 42 }
```

